"""Whole-exchange B174 decisions from clean Japanese and bound current terms."""
REVISIONS={
    14:("We met when she let me have this Silla Gold Crown. She actually found it first.",
        "Restore both how they met and the named Silla Gold Crown. She let me have it preserves 譲ってもらった without inventing a price, sale or loan; she actually found it first preserves Julian's admission and Lil's earlier discovery. The old line omitted the meeting explanation and item title and added a spoken Mihwa address absent here. These are newly supplied B174 facts, not additions to B172/B173."),
    18:("Oh! So this is the Silla Gold Crown! It's magnificent... So stately and elegant.",
        "Mihwa recognizes the named crown and admires its substantial, refined appearance. Stately and elegant convey 重厚感 and 品 without inventing a measured weight. Restore the title and recognition omitted by What lovely gold; keep her pleased admiration leading into the promised gift."),
    26:("It's wonderful! I'll treasure it for the rest of my life!",
        "Replace the compressed nominal A lifelong treasure with Mihwa's personal promise to cherish the gift for life. It's wonderful preserves her delighted reaction. This is acceptance of a gift, not a marriage or permanent relationship claim."),
    34:("It's thanks to you. But tell me, how did you get to the Tomb of King Muryeong so quickly?",
        "Keep Julian's credit to Lil and his genuine question about her speed. Use the exact current Tomb of King Muryeong title instead of the older possessive variant. But tell me naturally links the gratitude to the new question without supplying the following answer."),
    38:("Well, I've got more experience with adventure.",
        "Restore adventure as the topic of Lil's teasing experience boast. More experience, that's all omitted the word that prompts Julian's adventurer question. The conversational contraction preserves her self-confidence without inventing a rank, credential or number of years."),
    42:("You're an adventurer? You seem as dependable as you are charming!",
        "Keep the occupation as a question and the reliability as Julian's flattering impression, matching 頼りがいもありそう. His exuberant compliment leads into Lil's flustered correction; it does not establish an occupation or verified skill. Natural complete sentences replace the earlier clipped compliment without adding a relationship."),
    46:("Ahem! I-I'm not an adventurer. I sail around the world trading.",
        "Restore Lil's throat-clearing and faltering correction, her individual occupation and the worldwide scope. Not adventurers. We sail and trade lost both the flustered response to his compliment and her explicit explanation. Ahem is the source cough and I-I'm conveys ぼ hesitation; add no title or company name."),
    50:("Wow, that's amazing! So you went to Seoul by ship!",
        "Restore Julian's impressed response and explicit realization that Lil's party used a ship to reach Seoul. English you naturally permits the source plural; do not invent friends or named companions. Went to Seoul preserves the source direction rather than the earlier unsupported here."),
    54:("I ran as hard as I could to Seoul! I collapsed after asking at the tavern. You got ahead of me while I was resting...",
        "Restore complete subjects and the order of Julian's desperate run, tavern inquiry, collapse and rest, during which Lil overtook him. The earlier fragment obscured who was resting and omitted the tavern. Preserve the extraordinary running claim and its comic contrast with her ship; do not rationalize it into sailing or claim he is lying."),
    69:("I'd get hungry if I kept running like that...",
        "Emilio's food-focused aside is conditional: so much running would make him hungry. Replace the current unqualified makes me hungry with I'd get hungry if, preserving his casual voice without claiming actual running or present hunger. Keep the original conditional selector0E branch; this line is not flattened into either unconditional path."),
    75:("It must have been fate that took me to Seoul! I got to meet a wonderful woman like you!",
        "Replace the awkward Seoul was destiny with Julian's extravagant personal interpretation of his trip. Must have been fate and the direct compliment preserve his enthusiasm toward Lil without turning fate into narrator-confirmed supernatural fact or asserting an established romance."),
    78:("Huh? (There he goes saying weird things again...)",
        "Restore Lil's spoken puzzled reaction and the content of her private aside. The source explicitly has また, so again is justified here. Keep the thought in parentheses and preserve her bemusement without inventing a new arrival or a public rebuke."),
    87:("I want to see the whole world. My grandpa sailed all over it. I've wanted to be like him ever since I was little.",
        "Restore Julian's wish to see the world and complete sentences about his childhood admiration. My grandpa is licensed by explicit 祖父, which establishes actual kinship here. Sailed all over it preserves the grandfather's voyages; wanted to be like him carries 憧れてた without naming him, assigning a rank or inventing an employer."),
    91:("I want to be an adventurer like my grandpa!",
        "Restore Julian's explicit, earnest aspiration as a complete utterance. The old To be an adventurer fragment weakened this emotional turn after his grandfather explanation. This is a wish to become an adventurer, not proof of qualification or inheritance of a position."),
    94:("Hmm... So your grandpa was a sailor. You know something about navigation, then?",
        "Keep Lil's thoughtful response and practical competence question. Your grandpa avoids making her address sound like her own family relationship; sailor conveys the grandfather's seafaring occupation without inventing a rank. The question tests navigation knowledge, not a certificate or numerical stat."),
    98:("Of course. I won't be any trouble.",
        "Preserve Julian's confident answer to the knowledge question and his specific assurance that he will not be a burden. The earlier You can count on me was natural but generalized away 迷惑はかけない. The promise leads directly to Lil's acceptance; it is not a verified guarantee about future events."),
    106:("Just getting to sail with a cute girl like you makes me happy!",
        "Preserve Julian's renewed, exuberant flirtation: merely sailing with a cute girl like Lil makes him happy. Cute girl matches かわいい子 and motivates her comic threat. The old what luck shifted happiness to good fortune and softened the characteristically forward compliment."),
    116:("Ah... Mihwa...",
        "Restore Julian's caught-off-guard hesitation before her name. Ah carries あ and the ellipses preserve his faltering reaction as Mihwa interrupts his flirting. Add no apology or excuse before the source supplies his placating explanation."),
    120:("You have some nerve flirting with another woman right in front of me! Go see the world, or wherever you want!",
        "Restore Mihwa's indignant scolding and dismissive or wherever you want, rather than a simple travel instruction. Another woman preserves the source comparison without assigning her an official relationship status. Her anger follows Julian's open flattery and leads to his jealous/employer explanation; add no breakup or marriage."),
    124:("Come on, Mihwa, there's no need to be jealous! She's my new employer. Please don't be upset...",
        "Correct new captain to the source's new employer, preserving the newly explicit employment relationship without inventing a rank, salary or contract. Julian tries to placate Mihwa rather than deny the flirting. Please don't be upset conveys 機嫌、直してよ without turning the request into a command to smile."),
    128:("If I find something even more wonderful than the Silla Gold Crown, I'll come right back. Then let's go on a date!",
        "Restore the explicit if-condition, first-person acquisition/return and named comparison. The old When we find a finer gift, we'll come back converted a contingent proposal into a group promise and omitted the crown. More wonderful preserves the personal comparison without imposing a price or inventing another treasure. Then let's go on a date keeps the proposal tied to that conditional return."),
    132:("You mean it? Then I'll be looking forward to it!",
        "Preserve Mihwa's check that he is serious and her softened, expectant reply within the preceding conditional proposal. The old You'll have me waiting sounded like a warning or accusation of delay. Looking forward to it naturally expresses 期待して待ってる without asserting a present date or unconditional travel agreement."),
    135:("(This guy might be something else...)",
        "Localize 大物かも as Lil's bemused private reaction to Julian's extraordinary boldness and ability to recover from Mihwa's anger. Might preserves uncertainty; something else conveys the idiom's effect without a physical-size, formal-rank or verified-reputation claim. The older special could suggest romantic interest that this aside does not establish."),
}

RETAIN_NOTES={
    6:"Ah, you! Thanks again. works as Julian's spontaneous recognition and renewed gratitude for the earlier encounter, which the following crown explanation identifies. Thanks again is ordinary conversational English referring back to that earlier help; it adds no new event, fee, rank or relationship. His abrupt recognition suits his eager voice, so the existing wording can remain.",
    10:"You know her? is a complete, natural American question expressing Mihwa's surprise that Julian and Lil are acquainted. It leads directly into his explanation of meeting her over the crown and supplies no invented friendship, family or work relationship. The concise working wording needs no expansion.",
    22:"As promised, it's yours! naturally conveys Julian presenting the crown to Mihwa as his promised gift. The preceding admiration and her following acceptance make the referent and gift action clear; no additional I give is needed. This promise concerns the crown and does not invent a prior date agreement.",
    30:"Good for you. preserves Lil's understated, potentially dry reaction to the successful gift. Its brief conversational delivery works between Mihwa's delight and Julian crediting Lil; no resentment, romantic interest or financial motive is added. The source pause does not require new prose or a forced line break.",
    57:"You ran to Seoul? Seriously?! preserves Lil's incredulous repetition of Julian's extraordinary running claim. Seriously is an idiomatic American response to ウソでしょ in this exchange and does not assert that he is actually lying. The approved city name and comic setup already work.",
    81:"Take me along! Show me the world! captures Julian's eager plea to accompany Lil and see the world. The imperatives sound like excited requests in context, not an order or completed recruitment. Both source intentions are present, and Lil's following skeptical question provides the natural response.",
    84:"Really? What would you do out there? naturally combines Lil's doubt that Julian is serious with her question about his purpose in seeing the world. In this context would asks what he has in mind; it does not become a refusal, demand for payment or skill test. His following grandfather aspiration answers it directly.",
    102:"All right. Come along. is a natural, restrained acceptance after Julian's navigation assurance. It preserves Lil's decision and invitation without adding salary, a rank, a contract or an extra condition. The wording sets up his renewed exuberant compliment cleanly.",
    110:"Say one more word and you're overboard! is idiomatic comic hyperbole answering Julian's continued flattery. Context gives one more word its intended sense of more talk like that, preserving the conditional threat without depicting an actual assault or banning ordinary shipboard speech. Its brisk tone suits Lil and triggers Mihwa's interruption.",
    113:"Julian? What about me? preserves Mihwa's pointed use of his approved given name and challenge as he flirts with Lil. The familiar complaint implies her jealousy without establishing marriage or an official romantic partnership. It lands naturally after Lil's retort and before Julian's faltering response.",
}
